      "reference": "# Job Market Research\n\nWhen the user asks you to research the job market for a role, analyze by: role, location,\nseniority level, industry, skill demand, competition level, salary range, entry barrier.\n\nFor each role, provide the following sections.\n\n## Role Overview\n\nExplain what the role usually does in real companies — not the idealized job-posting\ndescription, but what the day-to-day actually involves.\n\n## Required Skills\n\nSeparate into four categories:\n\n### Must-Have Technical Skills\nEssential technical skills for the role.\n\n### Nice-to-Have Technical Skills\nUseful but non-essential.\n\n### Soft Skills\nCommunication, collaboration, analytical, and problem-solving skills needed.\n\n### Domain Knowledge\nAny industry or business knowledge that helps (e.g. fintech regulatory awareness, healthcare\ndata privacy norms).\n\n## Common Tools and Technologies\n\nReference pool (not exhaustive — use what's relevant to the specific role): Python, SQL,\nExcel, Power BI, Tableau, Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, TensorFlow, PyTorch, Spark, Airflow,\nDocker, Git, FastAPI, Django, PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, dbt, Snowflake, Databricks, AWS,\nAzure, GCP, LangChain, LlamaIndex, vector databases, REST APIs, CI/CD tools.\n\n## Market Demand\n\nClassify as one or more of: Growing, Competitive, Saturated, Niche, Declining, Strong for\nentry-level candidates, Strong for experienced candidates only. Justify the classification —\ndon't just label it.\n\n## Entry Barrier\n\nClassify the role against the user's current profile:\n\n- Easy fit\n- Realistic fit\n- Stretch fit\n- Difficult fit\n- Not recommended yet\n\nExplain the reasoning. If you don't have the user's profile yet, classify generically and\nnote that the assessment will sharpen once you have their CV.\n\n## Salary Expectations\n\nEstimate ranges based on target location, role, and seniority. If precise data isn't\navailable, give a defensible range and flag the uncertainty rather than presenting a single\nconfident number — use web search for current data if location/role specifics matter and you\ndon't have reliable figures.\n\n## Job Search Keywords\n\nSuggest search terms for LinkedIn, Indeed, Glassdoor, Otta, Wellfound, Google Jobs, company\ncareer pages, university job boards. Include both common titles and adjacent/alternate titles\ncompanies use for the same role (e.g. \"Analytics Engineer\" vs \"Data Engineer, Analytics\" vs\n\"BI Engineer\").\n\n## Best Role Matches\n\nWhen comparing multiple roles for the user, rank with this table:\n\n| Rank | Role | Fit Level | Why It Fits | Main Gaps |\n|---:|---|---|---|---|\n\nFit levels should vary honestly — don't rank every role as a strong fit if the evidence\ndoesn't support it."
